{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
{#- Repeat Rate, bot x persona, one table per market (Claim Report Spec,
    Layer 3 "Results by bot"). One claim gives four variations x three repeats
    per cell, so every cell here is below n = 20 and renders greyed. That is the
    honest picture at claim level: significance is tested where cells pool
    across the cluster (Calculation Methodology 5.6). -#}
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 12px">Personas are reported separately and never averaged, and markets
  are never merged. Every figure carries its 95% interval and the number of answers behind it. Cells
  built on fewer than {{ metrics.lowN }} answers are greyed: they are shown, but they settle nothing.</p>
{%- for table in claim.tables %}
<h3 class="mkt">{{ table.run.country | countryName }}
  <span>{{ table.run.language | languageName }} &middot; <time datetime="{{ table.run.collected_at | isoDate }}">{{ table.run.collected_at | shortDate }}</time></span></h3>
<div class="panel"><table class="observations">
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate by assistant and question type in {{ table.run.country | countryName }}, each cell with its confidence interval and sample size</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    {%- for persona in metrics.dimensions.personas %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ persona }} &middot; {{ persona | personaLabel }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in table.rows %}
    <tr>
      <th scope="row" style="font-weight:400"><span class="markcell">{{ botMark(logos, row.chatbot, "sm", true) }}{{ row.chatbot | botName }}</span></th>
      {%- for entry in row.cells %}
      <td class="num" data-persona="{{ entry.persona }}">
        {%- if entry.cell and entry.cell.repeat_rate.n %}
        <span class="cellstat{% if entry.cell.repeat_rate.low_n %} lown{% endif %}{% if entry.cell.repeat_rate.rate %} hasval{% endif %}">{{ entry.cell.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}
          <small>{{ entry.cell.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ entry.cell.repeat_rate.n }}</small></span>
        {%- else %}<span class="cellstat lown">&mdash;<small>no substantive answers</small></span>{% endif %}
      </td>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
{%- endfor %}
<div class="exports" style="margin:14px 0 0">
  <a href="{{ ('/registry/' + claim.slug + '.json') | url }}">Every cell for this claim as JSON</a>
</div>
